<newsitem itemid="470715" id="root" date="1997-03-26" xml:lang="en">
<title>UK: Barratt first-half pretax profit up 30 pct.</title>
<headline>Barratt first-half pretax profit up 30 pct.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to Dec 31</p>
<p>		 (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		7.0		    vs 6.5</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 3.0		    vs 2.75</p>
<p> Pretax		     24.8		   vs 19.1</p>
<p> Turnover		   311.2		  vs 277.2</p>
<p> Operating profit	 26.1		   vs 23.2</p>
<p>NOTE - Analyst profit forecasts for Britain's second largest housebuilder were between 23.5 and 25.2 million stg before tax and a dividend of three pence a share.</p>
<p>Barratt Developments Plc said it had restated the 1995 H1 dividend and earnings per share figures to reflect its one-for-four rights issue a year ago.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
